{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"<system-reminder>This memory is 15 days old. Memories are point-in-time observations, not live state — claims about code behavior or file:line citations may be outdated. Verify against current code before asserting as fact.</system-reminder>\n1\t---\n2\tname: evintunador-workflow-preferences\n3\tdescription: \"How the user wants Claude to work — subagents for economy, intent questions before building\"\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: feedback\n7\t  originSessionId: c158a677-efd7-4ff4-87ac-1c3052566c2e\n8\t  modified: 2026-07-19T07:14:23.185Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tThe user asked (2026-07-19) to save context window and subscription rate\n12\tlimits by delegating to sub-agents of lesser models (haiku/sonnet) where\n13\tapplicable, and to ask clarifying questions about their *intent* before\n14\tbuilding — they expect the right questions to significantly shift the design,\n15\tand they answer them thoughtfully (often via the \"Other\" free-text option).\n16\t\n17\t**Why:** they are on a rate-limited subscription and treat the main-model\n18\tcontext as a scarce resource; they also treat design docs as provisional and\n19\texpect intent to be re-derived through dialogue rather than followed blindly.\n20\t\n21\t**How to apply:** fan out exploration/research/format-reverse-engineering to\n22\tbackground haiku/sonnet agents in parallel; keep the main context for\n23\tsynthesis, decisions, and precision coding. Before implementing a new\n24\tproject, present findings and ask 3-4 sharp intent questions\n25\t(AskUserQuestion) whose answers change the architecture. Related:\n26\t[[turnbridge-mvp-decisions]].\n27\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GyVmsMq71kPRhmUqWrBitT","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"173cfc66bb28f4c20e474f522f197eeef0c627de","repo":"git@github.com