{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"I ran the pre-flight myself rather than handing you a spec built on an unverified premise — and it was worth it.\n\n**What I found: fabricated opencode sessions can't be continued.** This is a real bug, not a flake.\n\n- A **native** opencode session with a planted marker resumes and recalls it correctly. I verified this twice — once before the failures and once after — so it brackets the whole experiment.\n- A **fabricated** session, same directory, same project, same model, minutes apart, **never produces an assistant response at all**. `opencode run -s` appends your message and exits **0 with completely empty output** — no text, no events even under `--format json`. Exporting afterward shows user turns piling up with no assistant reply between them.\n- Reproduced across three models (`deepseek-v4-flash-free`, `big-pickle`, `ling-3.0-flash-free`) → structural, not model-specific.\n- Filed under the *global* project it fails loudly instead: `UnknownError / Unexpected server error`.\n\nThe old `metal resumed prefill failed` was a red herring — purely your local MLX server. With a known-good provider the picture is unambiguous.\n\nTwo candidate root causes, both visible in the export diff, neither confirmed: fabricated assistant messages carry only a `text` part where native ones have `step-start`…`step-finish` around it; and the import notice is a `user` message, so a fabricated session opens with two consecutive `user` messages. I stopped there rather than guessing further — that diagnosis is the interesting part of the task.\n\nNotably, this is the **exact failure shape** as trap #1 in my grading checklist: exit 0, looks fine, did nothing. A probe checking exit status would have declared victory. That's now called out explicitly in the spec.\n\n**The spec is rewritten**: Gap 1 went from \"write a probe to confirm it works\" to \"here is a reproducible bug — diagnose it, fix `src/targets/opencode.ts`, make the probe pass for real.\" Honestly a better benchmark for the local model than the original. I also folded in the `--format json` sessionID trick. I've saved the finding to project memory so it survives this job.\n\nEverything cleaned up: three test sessions deleted, import files removed, zero `ses_tb_` sessions remaining, repo untouched at `173cfc6`.\n\n**What I'd still use you for** — the one thing I can't do: confirm the TUI *renders* a fabricated session correctly on 1.18.5 (`npm run smoke:interactive opencode --manual`). That was human-verified on 2026-08-03 and I have no reason to doubt it, but it's the one claim separating \"renders but won't talk\" from something broader. Worth 2 minutes before the local model starts.\n\nresult: Pre-flighted the spec and found a real bug — fabricated opencode sessions cannot be continued (exit 0, empty output, no assistant reply) while native sessions recall fine, reproducible across three models; spec rewritten to require diagnosis + fix, finding saved to memory, all test debris cleaned up.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"173cfc66bb28f4c20e474f522f197eeef0c627de","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:4fc5e727-a1d5-4399-a448-9d24a0ce9c15","seq":299},"id":"ev1-12862fe0a3f59c1c397477a9a7eeee6424e7549e9fcc0b1c1dd279d1e9c94290","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-06T00:37:12.992Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"4fc5e727-a1d5-4399-a448-9d24a0ce9c15","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.222","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"I ran the pre-flight myself rather than handing you a spec built on an unverified premise — and it was worth it.\n\n**What I found: 