y excluded — policy unchanged.\n\n**0.6.0 — re-normalization (`6526090`)**\n- New library exports: `renormalize()`, type `RenormalizeResult` (`src/index.ts` diff, `src/renormalize.ts` new file).\n- New CLI command: `cledger renormalize`.\n- Turns preserved `unrecognized` events this cledger version can now parse into `conversation_turn` + appends a `supersession` event (`links:[{rel:\"supersedes\", target}]`). Id-fidelity: reconstructed turn gets the exact id a live capture would produce, so future live capture dedups.\n- Opt-in/manual only — must be invoked explicitly (`cledger renormalize`), not run automatically. Not a default-behavior change by itself, but its output (new `conversation_turn` + `supersession` events) is a new steady-state a reader must expect once someone runs it.\n\n**0.6.1 — mask matched span (`54bb44b`)**\n- Internal to `src/redact/scan.ts` (finding-report formatting only). No API/schema/CLI surface change. Not consumer-relevant.\n\n**0.7.0 — known-secrets store (`33f522b`)**\n- New config key `{\"redact\": {\"knownSecrets\": true}}`, opt-in/off by default. Local-only store at `.git/conversation-ledger/known-secrets.json`.\n- No new exported functions/types in `src/index.ts`. `cli.ts` and `store.ts`/`redact/apply.ts`/`redact/known-secrets.ts` touched internally.\n- Behavior note: enabling this makes capture machine-dependent for remembered values (different event ids on machines without the value cached) — same caveat as pre-existing env-masking.\n\n**0.7.1 — hardening (`1ddda10`)**\n- Tightens the sync-scan keyword-assignment regex (fewer false positives) and fixes 0.7.0's store perms (0600 enforced/repaired on write; previously landed 0644). No public API change.\n\n**0.8.0 — re-anchoring (`d3934db`, `c36b4b5`, `a452048`)**\n- **New event kind**: `re_anchor` added to `KNOWN_KINDS` (`src/schema.ts`, commit `d3934db`). A mapping event asserting rewritten-away commits (squash/rebase) live on in a successor commit. Anchored to the successor, deterministic id (sorted SHAs + system actor).\n- **New exports** (`src/index.ts`): `runReAnchor`, `manualReAnchor`, `defaultRewriteTarget`, `detectRewrites`, `parseReAnchor`, `reAnchorDraft`; types `ReAnchorRunResult`, `DetectedRewrite`, `DetectRewritesResult`, `ReAnchorMapping`, `ReAnchorDraftOptions`, `UnmatchedBranch`.\n- **New CLI command**: `cledger re-anchor` (dry-run default, `--apply`, manual `<old-rev...> --onto REV`).\n- **`appendEvents` signature change (additive, non-breaking)**: `opts: { context?: RepoContext }` → `opts: { context?: RepoContext; anchor?: string }` (`src/store.ts`). Optional param, source-compatible.\n- **`readEvents` reachability semantics changed**: previously `opts.reachableFrom` did plain `git rev-list` filtering; now (`resolveAnchors` in `store.ts`) it resolves `re_anchor` mappings to a fixpoint so squash-orphaned anchors \"revive.\" This is a **behavior change on default reads** — a downstream consumer's reachable-event set can now include events anchored to commits that are not actually reachable via plain git history, once a mapping exists.\n- **DEFAULT-ON SIDE EFFECT (important for turnbridge)**: `readEvents()` now also calls `autoReAnchor(repo)` (`c36b4b5`) on every invocation. This can **write** a `re_anchor` event to the git-notes ledger (via `appendEvents`) as a side effect of what turnbridge treats as a read-only call (`listConversations`, `readLineage` in turnbridge both call `readEvents`). Gated by a tip cursor file at `<gitDir>/conversation-ledger/reanchor-cursor` (only re-runs detection when the target branch's tip moved), never throws, and prints progress/ambiguity messages to `stderr`. Opt-out: `{\"reanchor\": {\"auto\": false}}` in `.cledger.json`/`~/.config/cledger/config.json`. New `CledgerConfig.reanchor` config section (`src/redact/config.ts`).\n- `SCHEMA_VERSION` string (\"conversation-ledger/v1\") was **not** bumped despite the new `re_anchor`/`unrecognized` kinds — kinds are treated as open/extensible, not schema-version-gated.\n\n**0.9.0 — evidence-ranked suggestions + forge abstraction (`62757ac`, `61c9c89`, `695dad4`)**\n- New files `src/forge/forge.ts`, `src/forge/github.ts`, `src/reanchor-suggest.ts`.\n- **New exports**: `suggestMappings`, `forgeForRepo`; types `BranchSuggestions`, `Suggestion`, `ForgeDriver`, `ForgePullRequest`.\n- `ForgeDriver.pullRequestsForBranch(branch)` — GitHub driver over the user's `gh` CLI session (no credential handling by cledger itself; 10s timeout; degrades to `null` rather than throwing on missing/unauthenticated `gh`, non-GitHub origin, offline).\n- `detectRewrites`/`UnmatchedBranch` extended to report non-exact matches (previously just dropped) with a `noted` commit subset (`695dad4` fix, so the confirm-command doesn't accidentally drop the anchor commit).\n- Forge lookups run **only** inside the explicit `cledger re-anchor` command, never in the automatic read-time path (`autoReAnchor` stays offline) — so this doesn't add new default-path network calls, but it does mean `cledger re-anchor` (interactive/manual use) can now shell out to `gh`.\n- Opt-out: `--no-forge` flag / `{\"reanchor\": {\"forge\": false}}`.\n- `695dad4` is a same-day follow-up bugfix to `62757ac`'s output (not a separate version bump).\n\n## 3. Breaking / behavior-changing items a consumer must react to\n\n1. **New event kinds `re_anchor` (0.8.0) and `unrecognized` (0.5.0), plus `supersession` usage growth (0.6.0)** — any code that enumerates `readEvents()` output without an explicit `kind:` filter must now tolerate these. Turnbridge is currently safe here: `src/conversations.ts` and `src/lineage.ts` both pass an explicit `kind` filter (`\"conversation_turn\"` / `CONTINUATION_KIND`) to `readEvents`, so these extra kinds are filtered out — **no actual code fix needed**, but worth confirming this remains true if turnbridge ever calls `readEvents` without a kind filter.\n2. **`readEvents()` now has write side effects (0.8.0, `c36b4b5`)** — every call may append a `re_