# pick a conversation from this repo's history and resume it anywhere\nturnbridge resume            # interactive: choose conversation, then target CLI\nturnbridge resume codex      # resume straight into Codex\nturnbridge resume claude     # resume straight into Claude Code\nturnbridge list              # print compatible conversations\n\n# options\n#   --all         include collaborators' conversations\n#   --any-commit  include conversations from other branches/commits\n#   --bootstrap   force transcript rehydration instead of native fabrication\n\n# optional: make bare `claude --resume` / `codex resume` open the merged picker\nturnbridge shim install\n```\n\nSame-CLI selections use the CLI's native resume. Cross-CLI selections write a\ntarget-native session file and hand off to the target's own resume; when that\nis unsupported for the installed CLI version, turnbridge falls back to a fresh\nsession bootstrapped with the literal transcript.\n\nSee [product intent](docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md) and the [WIP technical design](docs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md).\n\n## Development\n\n```sh\nnpm install   # links ../conversation-ledger\nnpm test      # build + node --test\n```\n\n## License\n\n[MIT](LICENSE)\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge/README.md","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49},"type":"text"},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"74ecfa5e-5f22-4a4c-83de-ed6b2fc1c7c6","version":"2.1.216"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-08-11T02:16:45.305Z","schema":"conversation-ledger/v1"}
{"actor":{"type":"system"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# WIP technical design\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** MVP implemented for Claude Code ⇄ Codex; fabrication adapters are\n4\tversion-pinned and must be revalidated per CLI release.\n5\t\n6\t## Main flow\n7\t\n8\t1. Conversation Ledger's hooks (`cledger install all`) capture each CLI's\n9\t   local transcript incrementally into git notes as normalized\n10\t   `conversation_turn` events, stamped with the repo's git identity\n11\t   (`actor.id` = `user.email`) on human turns.\n12\t2. `turnbridge resume [claude|codex]` lists conversations compatible with the\n13\t   current repository state: events anchored to commits reachable from `HEAD`\n14\t   (`--any-commit` lifts this), authored by you or unattributed\n15\t   (`--all` includes collaborators).\n16\t3. Selecting a conversation whose source matches the target CLI delegates to\n17\t   that CLI's native resume.\n18\t4. Cross-CLI selections default to **native fabrication**: turnbridge writes a\n19\t   target-native session file from the canonical events and launches the\n20\t   target's own resume on it. `--bootstrap` (also the automatic fallback when\n21\t   fabrication is unsupported or fails validation) starts a fresh target\n22\t   session whose first prompt instructs it to read the literal transcript.\n23\t\n24\t## Module map\n25\t\n26\t- `src/conversations.ts` — ledger read + grouping + ownership/compat filter.\n27\t- `src/resume.ts` — picker flow, target choice, default-target config.\n28\t- `src/targets/*` — per-CLI `TargetAdapter`: `nativeResume`, `fabricate`,\n29\t  `bootstrap`. Fabrication throws `FabricationUnsupportedError` to trigger the\n30\t  fallback.\n31\t- `src/transcript.ts` + `src/bootstrap.ts` — literal markdown rendering and\n32\t  the rehydration prompt; reports estimated token size before launch.\n33\t- `src/shim.ts` — opt-in PATH shims: bare `claude --resume` / `codex resume`\n34\t  open the merged picker; everything else passes through to the real binary.\n35\t\n36\t## Division of labor with Conversation Ledger\n37\t\n38\tThe ledger owns capture (adapters, cursors, idempotent event ids, git-notes\n39\tstorage, explicit sync). Turnbridge never parses source transcripts itself and\n40\tis a reader plus a writer of *target-native* session files. It writes exactly\n41\tone kind of ledger event — `continuation` lineage edges (below) — and no\n42\tconversation content. Ledger changes made for turnbridge: a library entry\n43\tpoint (`package.json` exports) and human-turn identity stamping.\n44\t\n45\t## Conversation lineage (branch-on-bridge)\n46\t\n47\tBridging is a fork, not a move. Fabricating a target session writes a real\n48\tnative file; when the user continues there, the target CLI captures it as a\n49\tnew conversation whose id is the session id turnbridge generated (verified:\n50\tCodex resume preserves the id and appends). The source conversation still\n51\texists, so both are resumable — a genuine branch, like a git fork.\n52\t\n53\tTo keep that honest instead of confusing, at fabricate time turnbridge appends\n54\ta `continuation` event (`links: [{rel:\"continues\", target:<source>}]`, content\n55\tcarries `imported_through_seq`) belonging to the target conversation. The\n56\tpicker reads these and labels rows in both directions (`→ bridged to Codex`,\n57\t`↳ continued from Claude Code`); re-bridging a conversation that already\n58\tembeds imported history is allowed but flagged. The default listing shows\n59\tboth branch endpoints — abandonment is not assumed. The same edge is what lets\n60\ta downstream consumer (intent-recall) de-duplicate the copied prefix: target\n61\tturns `0..imported_through_seq` are known copies of the source, not fresh\n62\tevidence, so turnbridge does not need to alter capture to avoid double-count.\n63\t\n64\t## Fabrication contract (per target adapter)\n65\t\n66\t- Pin the CLI versions the writer was validated against; on an unknown version\n67\t  warn and offer bootstrap.\n68\t- Write only new session files under the CLI's own session directory; never\n69\t  modify existing native sessions.\n70\t- Represent foreign tool calls faithfully (or as clearly-labeled text when the\n71\t  target rejects unknown tool schemas — see per-adapter spec notes).\n72\t- Label the session as imported in its first visible message.\n73\t\n74\tReverse-engineered, empirically verified format specs (pinned versions,\n75\tminimal working schemas, unknowns): [docs/specs/claude-session-format.md](specs/claude-session-format.md)\n76\tand [docs/specs/codex-rollout-format.md](specs/codex-rollout-format.md).\n77\tKey constraints: Claude resume is scoped to the project dir encoded from the\n78\tlaunch cwd and reconstructs history by walking `parentUuid` from the last\n79\tline; Codex resume-by-id scans `~/.codex/sessions` for a matching filename +\n80\t`session_meta` id, and only plain `message` response_items are verified-safe\n81\tto replay (foreign tool calls fold into labeled text). Claude accepts foreign\n82\t`tool_use` names verbatim, so Codex→Claude keeps structured tool history.\n83\t\n84\t## Sharing model\n85\t\n86\t`actor.id`/`actor.display` come from `git config user.email/name` at capture\n87\ttime. Default listings: own + unattributed conversations; `--all` shows every\n88\tauthor with labels. Transport is Conversation Ledger's explicit `cledger sync`\n89\t(git notes push/fetch); turnbridge adds no network behavior. Events captured\n90\tbefore identity stamping existed are unattributed; a forced transcript rescan\n91\tafter the upgrade can duplicate those turns under new event ids.\n92\t\n93\t## Risks\n94\t\n95\tNative formats change without notice (fabrication is version-pinned, bootstrap\n96\tis the recovery path); transcript content can include secrets (ledger-side\n97\tredaction is still an open roadmap item — review before `cledger sync`); full\n98\thistories can exceed the target's context (size is reported before launch);\n99\tcrashes mid-turn leave partial capture, which the ledger tolerates by design.\n100\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fke2dq5giX6BGAhZfTGzBk","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","dirty_fingerprint":"bc65e878d80c1722a0adee9428cbf850f1d73e21ecfd82d0c4182876ebf93c10","head":"173cfc66bb28f4c20e474f522f197eeef0c627de","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:6b979ed9-e38e-4fea-b585-342bba5a333c#agent:a320d69d7506c9fa1","parent":"claude-code:6b979ed9-e38e-4fea-b585-342bba5a333c","seq":12},"id":"ev1-ef0e2c97a71857a07e8a414e72ec881e2bd25a7b39c2de98d461e98c909301d8","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-07-21T21:21:05.464Z","producer":{"session_id":"6b979ed9-e38e-4fea-b585-342bba5a333c","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.216","tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"agentId":"a320d69d7506c9fa1","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":true,"message":{"content":[{"content":"1\t# WIP technical design\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** MVP implemented for Claude Code ⇄ Codex; fabrication adapters are\n4\tversion-pinned and must be revalidated per CLI release.\n5\t\n6\t## Main flow\n7\t\n8\t1. Conversation Ledger's hooks (`cledger install all`) capture each CLI's\n9\t   local transcript incrementally into git notes as normalized\n10\t   `conversation_turn` events, stamped with the repo's git identity\n11\t   (`actor.id` = `user.email`) on human turns.\n12\t2. `turnbridge resume [claude|codex]` lists conversations compatible with the\n13\t   current repository state: events anchored to commits reachable from `HEAD`\n14\t   (`--any-commit` lifts this), authored by you or unattributed\n15\t   (`--all` includes collaborators).\n16\t3. Selecting a conversation whose source matches the target CLI delegates to\n17\t   that CLI's native resume.\n18\t4. Cross-CLI selections default to **native fab